WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:05.280
What happens when the mysterious machinations of&nbsp;
the Clockworks meet the humble tuna fish sandwich?&nbsp;

00:00:05.280 --> 00:00:09.120
Five ordinary tuna sandwiches on white&nbsp;
bread were prepared for testing. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:12.640
first sandwich was input on the setting&nbsp;
“Rough,” and produced a pile of wheat,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.640 --> 00:00:16.960
a pile of yeast, a puddle of water, and a&nbsp;
bloody, twitching segment of tuna muscle.&nbsp;

00:00:16.960 --> 00:00:20.960
The second sandwich went through the machinery on&nbsp;
the setting “coarse,” and produced a small loaf&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.960 --> 00:00:25.120
of bread, and several chunks of cooked tuna.
The next sandwich was placed in the machine&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.120 --> 00:00:28.960
on the setting 1:1, and produced a salmon&nbsp;
sandwich on rye bread, which a research&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.960 --> 00:00:33.680
assistant promptly ate and described as “okay.”
The next sandwich, input on the setting “Fine,”&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.680 --> 00:00:37.600
came out the other side as another tuna&nbsp;
sandwich. This time, however, the quality of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:41.920
both the tuna and the bread had significantly&nbsp;
improved, as well as its nutrient content.&nbsp;

00:00:41.920 --> 00:00:45.200
The final sandwich was run through the&nbsp;
machine on the setting “Very fine.”&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.200 --> 00:00:49.280
The output was a small loaf of bread, baked&nbsp;
in the shape of a hyper-realistic tuna fish.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.280 --> 00:00:52.560
When the door was opened, the bread began&nbsp;
to move as if swimming about the room.&nbsp;

00:00:52.560 --> 00:00:56.480
The fish loaf has escaped custody,&nbsp;
and is missing, presumed eaten.

